# .dockerignore — build context filter for runpod_worker/Dockerfile.
#
# The worker image does `COPY . /opt/wangp`, so without this file the build
# context is the whole working tree: ~57 MB of .git plus whatever weights,
# outputs and LoRAs a developer happens to have on disk (ckpts/ alone is
# 50-60 GB once MiniMax H3 has been pulled). Everything here is either
# regenerated inside the image or supplied at run time by the network volume.
#
# Docker matches these patterns against the FULL path relative to the context
# root, so a bare `ckpts` excludes only the top-level directory, and a nested
# match needs an explicit `**/`. That is why the __pycache__/*.pyc rules are
# written twice.
#
# This is the only file this worker adds outside runpod_worker/.

# --- version control and editor state ---------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# --- weights and other run-time data (mounted from the network volume) -------
# checkpoints_paths and loras_root in the rendered wgp_config.json point at
# /runpod-volume/{ckpts,loras}; the in-image /opt/wangp/{ckpts,loras} are empty
# fallbacks created by the Dockerfile.
ckpts
loras
loras_i2v
storage
samples
cache
tmp

# Any stray weight file anywhere in the tree. No tracked file in this repo uses
# these extensions (checked with `git ls-files`), so this cannot drop something
# the image needs -- but one forgotten 21 GB transformer in the working tree
# would otherwise be uploaded to the daemon on every build.
**/*.safetensors
**/*.ckpt
**/*.pt
**/*.pth
**/*.gguf
**/*.whl
**/*.zip

# --- generated output --------------------------------------------------------
# The worker writes to /tmp/wangp-out (WANGP_OUTPUT_DIR), never to these.
outputs
outputs2
gradio_outputs

# --- state the image must generate for itself, not inherit -------------------
# settings/: `import wgp` does os.mkdir("settings") (wgp.py:2549) and
#   get_default_settings() json.dump()s settings/<model_type>_settings.json
#   (wgp.py:3174). A stale copy from a developer's UI session would be read back
#   as this endpoint's defaults.
# wgp_config.json: config.ensure_wgp_config() renders the real one into
#   /opt/wangp/config/. A file at the repo root would be the one shared/api.py
#   treats as the default path (shared/api.py:1070), silently shadowing it.
# loras_url_cache*.json: a URL->local-file cache keyed to another machine's
#   lora_dir.
settings
wgp_config.json
loras_url_cache.json
loras_url_cache_v2.json
plugins_local.json

# Locally cloned plugins (the two patterns .gitignore uses). Plugin code from a
# developer's tree is not part of a reproducible worker image.
plugins/wan2gp-*
plugins/wangp-*

# ffmpeg binaries: the image installs the apt package and re-runs
# download_ffmpeg() itself. A Windows or macOS ffmpeg_bins/ from a developer's
# tree would land on PATH ahead of the Linux one (shared/ffmpeg_setup.py:64-81).
ffmpeg_bins
ffmpeg_quarantine

# --- python build/test droppings --------------------------------------------
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
**/*.pyc
*.pyo
**/*.pyo
.pytest_cache
**/.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
*.egg-info
**/*.egg-info
.venv
venv
env
.env
.env.*

# NOTE: finetunes/ is deliberately NOT excluded. It is gitignored, so it is
# absent from a fresh clone, but when it does exist it holds hand-written model
# definitions (small JSON) that an operator may have pinned the endpoint to.
